WEBVTT

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:20.110
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:20.110
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:20.110
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.410
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.410
Chapter 1

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:55.160
In March of Space Year 794,
Imperial Year 485...

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:00.000
...Imperial forces advanced
past the Iserlohn Corridor...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.900
...and rendezvoused in the Van-Fleet Starzone,
a part of Free Planets Alliance territory.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.960
Commodore...

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:12.560
What an inconvenient rank.

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:20.250
If I were a Vice Admiral, I could
have led a fleet of 10,000 ships...

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.020
...and made a larger contribution
to the outcome of these battles.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:32.180
I have a mere 40 cruisers, 130 destroyers, 25 gunboats, and 10 missile-ships under my command.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.910
Lord Reinhard, please
don't be so hasty.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:40.490
We cannot run a marathon
at a sprinter's speed.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.170
Look at that decrepit old
man, Grimmelshausen.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:48.220
You mean our fleet commander ?

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.630
Yes.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:53.510
He's lived four times
longer than I have...

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:58.560
...has a fleet 50 times larger than
I do, and he's still incompetent.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.650
All he does is raise the
average age of the admirals.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:07.330
Even when he disparages other people,
he's graceful and doesn't sound malicious...

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.310
...that's one of his virtues.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:20.070
It's almost time for us to attend the council
of admirals with that "high average age."

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.370
Oh well.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.310
My attendance will
lower the average age.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.210
That's the only good thing.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:31.560
In this starzone...

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:37.510
As a matter of convenience, we'll call it by the name the rebels use, Van-Fleet.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:46.560
Due to their adverse environment none of its eight planets were colonized, so it is uninhabited.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:52.370
The main reason is that the main and
permanent star, Van-Fleet, is unstable...

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:58.180
...and this will affect our
fleets' actions as well.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:05.430
We should presume that we cannot maintain fleet communications during tactical maneuvers.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.050
Right.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:12.610
Based on this consideration,
we'll place our fleets as follows.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.310
This will give us
a tactical advantage.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:24.330
Wait a minute.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:35.300
According to that placement,
my fleet is too far in the rear.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:40.410
Your fleet should wait in the
rear as an important reserve...

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:44.040
...and advance to the front
line as opportunities present.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.330
No, no, no.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:53.070
Though you try not to show it, I know
that you consider me to be a burden.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:57.520
I understand that you don't think a decrepit old
admiral like me can perform a satisfactory job.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:05.250
It's a waste of oxygen for an old
man like that to still be living.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.000
If he would retire soon and quit
being a burden to other people...

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.820
...he could at least live his
remaining years with dignity.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:21.240
If I can no longer be of use to the
Imperial Fleet, there is no point in living.

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:26.410
At this stage, I should make
a decision on my life and...

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:31.930
...to avoid being an inconvenience to
you all, take an honorable "retirement."

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.220
Please, please
calm down, Admiral.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.980
He won't live much longer.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.160
Give him as much freedom as
you can to do what he wants.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:44.480
Yes, Majesty.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:47.510
Alright, I understand.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.310
Now put the gun down.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.000
I'll leave the left
wing to your fleet.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.600
You'll flank the
enemy's right front.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:06:03.050
It's an important position as we
try to encircle our adversary's fleet.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:07.670
You're an accomplished commander;
I'm sure this will suit you.

00:06:08.580 --> 00:06:12.890
Can't he immediately understand
the tactical importance of this task ?

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.670
I guess he's in no
way up to the task.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:20.940
Oh, thank you very much.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:24.520
You're giving this
old man a workplace.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:26.290
Thank you,
thank you so much.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:30.580
Muckenberger...

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:34.610
He's actually making a battle strategy
with the Grimmelshausen Fleet...

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:37.190
...outside of the war
potential consideration.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:41.030
If I were him,
I'd do the same.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:44.110
But in that case, I'll also lose any
opportunity to make a name for myself.

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:46.650
The next item
on our agenda is...

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:59.790
...the estimated number and
placement of the rebel fleet...

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.460
This is what happened;

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:13.140
Muckenberger's having a hard
time pleasing Grimmelshausen.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.430
That old gentleman...

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.430
...was a military aide-de-camp when
Friedrich IV was the Imperial advisor...

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:24.200
...and I've heard he took care of the Kaiser
in matters that can't really be made public.

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:27.750
That's the reason the
Kaiser trusts him so much.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:33.150
It was quite a sight to see the look of annoyance on the dignity-conscious Muckenberger...

00:07:33.150 --> 00:07:35.470
...but I can't
just laugh about it.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:38.100
I don't want to be a part of his "good riddance" scheme.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:43.010
I must manipulate that old man and somehow
create a chance to accomplish something.

00:07:44.310 --> 00:07:47.780
We'll head to the fleet
flagship, the Ostfahlen.

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.110
Yes, sir.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:56.580
Who was the blond brat
behind Grimmelshausen ?

00:07:59.710 --> 00:08:03.710
I believe it was
Commodore Reinhard von Musel.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:06.500
Reinhard von Musel...

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:11.460
The brother of
Countess Grunewald ?

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:17.710
Commodore Musel is assigned
in the Grimmelshausen Fleet.

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.410
Are you reconsidering
his assignment ?

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:24.790
He's just a commodore,
where else would I place him ?!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:29.010
I'm the Chief Commander of the Imperial
Space Fleet, why would I care about him ?!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.910
I...I apologize !

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:40.310
It is a fact that the number
of cannons is quite lacking.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:45.060
But Your Excellency, Fleet Commander,
it's possible to make up for it through mobility.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:48.680
If we place gunboats here and move
them to this point ten hours later...

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.680
...we can expect twice the
results as we would get otherwise.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:55.380
Yes, yes.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.670
It's a good plan.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:01.890
That Grimmelshausen...

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:05.210
...even though he praised it,
he didn't use my proposal.

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:12.670
I'm used to antipathy and hostility, but
what is this lukewarm unresponsiveness ?

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:20.000
Kircheis, in this age of our Empire, imbecility,
incompetence, ignorance, and obstinacy...

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.730
...are clamoring a
cacophonous quartet.

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.110
The only reason we
haven't lost this war...

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:28.660
...is that our opponents are at
the same level of incompetence.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:32.240
If they had someone with even
one-tenth of my brain cells...

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:36.460
...Iserlohn Fortress would have
fallen into their hands decades ago.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:39.800
Dammit !

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:44.160
If I were the Fleet Admiral, if I were the
Chief Commander of the Space Fleet...

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.150
...I wouldn't have done
an imbecilic thing like this.

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:52.400
Wouldn't you turn down an able
subordinate's proposals, Lord Reinhard ?

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.340
Kircheis !

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.210
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.170
I hate lectures.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.610
I'm sorry.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:01.970
Why are you apologizing ?

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:06.120
You were giving me advice,
not lecturing me, weren't you ?

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.100
I was only kidding, Kircheis.

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.480
Yes, I know.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:15.550
Don't worry.

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:28.500
Our Commander, Commodore Musel,
has returned aboard.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.830
The brats have returned.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.890
Oh well, I guess today is
the last day of our lives.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:37.710
Our Fleet Commander is a
76 year old crock...

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:41.090
...and our Unit Commander
is an 18 year old greenhorn.

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:44.090
Makes me wonder what
our superiors are thinking.

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:46.870
If you average them out,
they're 47 years old.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.860
That's a workhorse age.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:49.760
Idiot.

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:52.820
An average doesn't
mean anything.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:55.590
Incompetent commanders are
more despicable than enemies.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:56.430
That's right.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:06.710
That pretty face is the
only thing going for him.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.560
What an aristocratic brat.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.280
Hey, they might hear you.

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:11.580
No way.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:15.150
There's a sound-proof field here
so we can't hear their voices...

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:16.940
...but that means they
can't hear ours either.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:17.820
Is that right ?

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.010
Well then.

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.110
You should have become a secretary
of the Imperial Household Agency...

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.210
...and stuffed your face
taking care of ballroom parties.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:27.070
Why did you bother to come
to the gory battlefield ?

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:30.970
You're only going to hurt your pretty little face out here.

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:34.080
You got pretty profane once you
found out they can't hear us.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:36.730
If I don't gripe about
it, I can't do my job.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:37.670
I agree with you.

00:11:50.800 --> 00:11:56.220
On March 11th at 2:40,
the first shots were fired.

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:59.520
The Battle of Van-Fleet
Starzone had begun.

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:09.340
But Reinhard's unit, in Grimmelshausen's
fleet, has not yet entered combat.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.660
<i>Fire !</i>

00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.310
Did you say something ?

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:22.590
Why haven't we been given
the order to open fire ?

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:25.770
80% of our fleet have
become like ghost ships.

00:12:26.780 --> 00:12:28.150
What would you do, Kircheis ?

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.430
Let's see.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:35.200
I would advance at least the Grimmelshausen
Fleet about 6 light seconds...

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:38.900
...then rotate them up to 2 o'clock and
concentrate our firepower on the target.

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:42.350
That way, we could deal significant
damage on the enemy's right front.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:43.960
You're right on the mark.

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:46.300
Brilliant, as usual.

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:50.660
Muckenberger belittles
Grimmelshausen...

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:55.620
...but Grimmelshausen's actions do
nothing to deny such an assessment.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:59.840
He's a burden and
it can't be helped.

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:01.710
Lord Reinhard...

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:06.610
...you lament the fact that you were
assigned to Vice Admiral Grimmelshausen...

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:08.710
...but there are scenarios...

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:12.770
...where you could suffer from the
aggressive malice of an inferior commander.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:16.380
You might consider your present
predicament undesirable but not the worst.

00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:21.960
There you go again with
your positive thinking.

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:42.430
But at 5:30, Grimmelshausen
ordered his fleet to advance.

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:46.860
The Grimmelshausen Fleet
has begun its advance.

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:51.820
What slow reactions
that old man has.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:54.730
His fleet is too
late to do any good.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.700
It's only a waste of energy.

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:16.970
Why are those slow footed
assault-landing ships positioned here ?

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:20.430
They're going to
hinder our movements.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:22.580
It's not just us.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:25.490
The movement of our
fleet is not uniform;

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:27.840
...our commanding and deployment
capabilities are in confusion.

00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:33.630
Grimmelshausen is lacking not
only in strategic capabilities...

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:36.930
...but also in overall planning
ability in regards to battle.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:41.550
Under whose command are those
assault-landing ships in front of us operating ?

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:47.340
Commodore Herman von
Luneberg of the marines.

00:14:47.340 --> 00:14:48.770
Call him up.

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:50.750
Open communications with
the assault-landing unit.

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:03.410
I am Commodore Reinhard von
Musel of the mobile fleet.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:07.560
Your assault-landing ships
are blocking our path.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.510
I ask that you give
us the right of way.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:16.920
We're in this position by the
order of the Fleet Commander.

00:15:16.920 --> 00:15:20.460
We cannot change our position
without his permission.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:23.710
If you want to move us...

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.220
...talk to the
Fleet Commander.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:30.380
What a rude man !

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.520
Lord Reinhard.

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:45.360
If our mission were to attack a
fortress or planet, I'd understand...

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:48.130
...but why are the
landing troops here ?

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.520
They're nothing but an eyesore.

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:58.770
But in this battle, the cuirassed fleet
of High Admiral Ovlessor is also present.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:02.970
I gather that the possibility of a
ground engagement is considered high.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:06.360
Ovlessor, eh ?

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:13.660
The rebels hate him and
call him "mincemeat maker."

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:15.010
Did you know that ?

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:16.100
Yes.

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:22.390
Kircheis, if you fought that "mincemeat
maker," you'd win, wouldn't you ?

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:24.780
I can't be
confident of it.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:27.080
You're so humble.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.350
You've never lost
at close combat.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:40.710
...has transpired.

00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:43.310
I'd like to report
that incident to you.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:50.300
My Lord, the brat has a
tendency to ignore our intentions.

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:51.820
What do you wish
to do about him ?

00:17:02.490 --> 00:17:04.310
What were you
talking about ?

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:11.860
We were talking
about that blond brat.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:16.640
Is there such a
person in our fleet ?

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:26.460
It's Commodore Reinhard von Musel,
the brother of Countess Grunewald.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:31.290
In the Commander's office, we were
laughing at him as the "blond brat."

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:43.520
That's not very
pleasing to hear.

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:47.770
Ah, yes, is that so ?

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:53.660
There's nothing wrong
with being a blond.

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:59.070
And it's not his
fault that he's young.

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:06.300
I don't agree with using such
matters as objects of derision.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.760
We can defend against
the enemy attack !

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:19.700
Here !

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:24.490
If we fire from this angle, we can cause
a cross fire with that of the main fleet...

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:26.820
...and dish out lots of
damage to the enemy fleet.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:31.170
That paragon of decrepitude can't even
understand something as easy as this.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:36.370
You don't have to be angry
like that, Lord Reinhard.

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:38.510
As incompetent
as they may be...

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:41.030
...those imbecilic superiors may
have a legitimate "raison d'etre."

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:42.580
"Raison d'etre" ?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.790
What kind of "raison d'etre"
do those imbeciles have ?

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.210
Is giving an undeserved
victory to the adversary...

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:51.870
...the legitimate "raison d'etre"
that you're talking about, Kircheis ?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.610
That's essentially what it is.

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.900
I get it now.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:04.420
What they lose, I'll recover.

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:08.960
On a relative scale,
my status will improve.

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:14.020
I see.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:22.670
Kircheis, I want victory, but I don't want it
because of the adversary's self-destruction.

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:24.160
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.400
Look, Kircheis.

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:30.950
That sun is the same
as the Galactic Empire.

00:19:30.950 --> 00:19:36.350
On the surface, it glistens like gold and
looks elegant, but inside, it's a rotten black.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:48.580
I wish I'd been born when Rudolph
von Goldenbaum was on the throne.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.580
If I had been, I would have
had all the enemies I wanted.

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:57.140
What I'm facing now are incompetent
allies and equally incompetent enemies.

00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:04.760
At this rate, I could perhaps dominate
the whole of space in ten years or so.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.250
Lord Reinhard !

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:09.120
Yes, I know, Kircheis.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:11.510
Overconfidence is the worst enemy.

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:15.990
I'm still just a
commander of 100 ships.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:19.410
I guess it's ridiculous for
me to talk so ambitiously.

00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:30.600
On March 24, the battlefield
had become even more chaotic.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:34.560
Both the Imperial and
Alliance fleets...

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:39.560
...had divided and isolated each other;
both sides got mixed up in disorder...

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:44.400
...and it got increasingly more difficult
to grasp the positioning of the fleets.

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:52.580
Both Imperial and Alliance fleets used a large
portion of their ships to advance upward.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:57.850
In other words, the ships would circumvent
the periphery of the enemy fleet to its rear...

00:20:57.850 --> 00:21:01.020
...in an attempt to attack
it from both front and rear.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:05.920
If successful, it would be recorded
in history as a daring strategy.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:10.290
Of course,
"if" it succeeds.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.860
Upward advancement by the fleet...

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:17.950
...it's a strategy that you'd
be eager to try, isn't it ?

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.390
It's impossible
for Muckenberger.

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:28.020
In fact, neither our allies nor our enemies have
any idea where the others are positioned...

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:31.610
...and are blindly executing
their own game plans.

00:21:31.610 --> 00:21:33.310
That won't work.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:34.640
I wholeheartedly agree.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:38.400
What're our allies doing ?

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.360
Can't they keep
up with our unit ?

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:44.980
At this rate, our unit alone
will project out and be isolated.

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:48.240
Dammit.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:49.870
It can't be helped.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:51.540
Slow down our
forward movement.

00:21:52.230 --> 00:21:55.240
This is like a thoroughbred
accompanying a turtle.

00:21:55.240 --> 00:21:58.560
Even if we're making
movements to our advantage...

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:00.470
...other units aren't keeping
up and that won't do.

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:03.010
Look at that.

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:04.760
The enemy fleet.

00:22:04.760 --> 00:22:08.930
The prey is passing by in front of
us and I can't do anything about it.

00:22:11.770 --> 00:22:16.460
Kircheis, there won't be a
one-sided victory in this battle.

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:18.960
If either side
concentrates its forces...

00:22:18.960 --> 00:22:21.760
...that would amass enough firepower
to destroy their adversary...

00:22:21.760 --> 00:22:24.340
...but both sides are using too many of
their ships in a meaningless circumvention...

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:26.820
...and their forces are
scattered all over the place.

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:32.490
It's not a suitable strategy in a place like this,
where communications are difficult to maintain.

00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:36.130
It's about time for both our allies
and enemies to realize that, isn't it ?

00:22:36.130 --> 00:22:37.480
I would think so.

00:22:37.480 --> 00:22:43.200
The rebels, who call themselves the "Alliance,"
are desperately trying to come up with ideas...

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:46.010
...to dig out their legs
that are stuck in the bog.

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:49.040
That's the price they have to pay for entering
a battle without a clear winning formula.

00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:52.560
6th Fleet flagship,
Pergamonn, respond.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.970
5th Fleet flagship,
Rio Grande, respond.

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:00.870
12th Fleet flagship,
Perun, respond.

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:08.360
We haven't had communications
with the 6th Fleet, have we ?

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:10.350
The 12th Fleet
has also disappeared.

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:13.770
The estimated location
of the 5th Fleet is here.

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:15.310
This data is
old and useless !

00:23:15.650 --> 00:23:17.430
This, and this, too !

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:20.690
If we can't communicate,
there's nothing we can do.

00:23:21.330 --> 00:23:23.750
Fleet Headquarters
will be isolated.

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:25.780
We should reassemble our fleet.

00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:27.340
But how ?

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:31.010
It's not time-effective, but we'll have
to send communications using shuttles.

00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:44.180
An order to return ?

00:23:44.180 --> 00:23:47.920
It says that at this rate,
Fleet Headquarters will be isolated.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:50.560
But if we turn and head
back from this position...

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:56.730
...we'll meet head on with the main Imperial Fleet and then be flanked by their detached fleet.

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:59.360
We should ignore
such an order.

00:23:59.360 --> 00:24:03.170
But we can't just ignore an order
from Fleet Headquarters, can we ?

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:04.560
What are we going
to say to them, Admiral ?

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:07.510
"We're lost."

00:24:07.510 --> 00:24:08.870
Huh ?

00:24:08.870 --> 00:24:12.810
"The 5th Fleet is lost"...

00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:15.410
...is what you
have to tell them.

00:24:15.410 --> 00:24:17.430
No, actually, there's
no need to tell them.

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:19.690
I don't want the enemy
to know that, either.

00:24:19.690 --> 00:24:23.970
Offer some drinks to the shuttle crew, and have them rest here.

00:24:28.530 --> 00:24:32.290
As a matter of outcome, the decision
by Bucock turned out to be judicious.

00:24:32.290 --> 00:24:39.410
And it would later play a key role
in the denouement of this battle...

00:24:38.760 --> 00:24:45.210
The Battle of Van-Fleet Starzone

00:24:39.410 --> 00:24:42.130
...but no one knew
that at this juncture.

00:24:47.010 --> 00:24:56.210
 Even as I say it's beautiful. Even as I say it's magnificent

